/**
 * Journals records (Phase 3) — the single validated content source
 * for journals.
 *
 * Generated by /tmp/gen-journals-records.mts from the frozen pre-move
 * exports (see __fixtures__/main-7c04e3a7.json, captured from the old
 * adapter + answers by /tmp/freeze-journals.mts). Content bytes come
 * from those inputs only: do not hand-edit a record here, and do not
 * retype one. The records are verified by the frozen-fixture test in
 * records.test.ts.
 *
 * Each record is one SubjectItem: the UnitItem fields (contract I2)
 * plus its answer, provenance, media rules and lead policy. Screens
 * read projections of these records (journalUnits, journalAnswers);
 * they never join files by hand. Provenance is UNVERIFIED for all 16
 * records: no verifiedOn date exists for these rows. Media is empty
 * for all 16: journals carries captions, not clip or still ids, in
 * its records (caption files resolve through the adapter below).
 * Lead policy is answer-not-in-lead for every record.
 *
 * Two records ask a year-gap question (technology:first-phone,
 * modern-world:liverpool-manchester). Their answer text is a
 * template: {year} is the current year and {years} the gap, filled
 * by the generator in answers.ts from the item's anchor year (the
 * named constants there). No current year is ever stored — the
 * projected answers at any year are computed at play time, exactly
 * as the old journalAnswers(year) computed them. The other two
 * date answers (Lincoln Memorial, mobile phone) are fixed gaps
 * between stored dates, so their records hold the finished entry.
 *
 * A row that carries a 10-18 `stretch` becomes its own record (the
 * stretch question and answer), in deal order: 8 / 7 / 1 per band.
 *
 * The clips adapter stays below the records: docs/scaling/journals
 * rows are never edited here, two curated rows are not in the live
 * slice yet (great-leaders:jhansi-fort, great-leaders:netaji-bhawan),
 * and caption lookup (captionRefFor) still reads the rows at run
 * time. The records above were generated from the adapter's output;
 * its override tables stay as the derivation record.
 */
